1
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,720
Can you believe it?

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,160
I bagged an A on the test.

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:06,700
How'd you do?

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,080
No big deal.

5
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:11,140
Uh, A -plus?

6
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,920
Made some lucky guesses.

7
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,960
In algebra? It's not like math is an exact science.

8
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,180
Okay, I'll get a B next time.

9
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:23,360
It's Sasha Sierotsky.

10
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,320
Today's the day Sasha's gonna ask me to the Sadie Hawkins dance.

11
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:27,260
How do you know?

12
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,980
Well, it's the payoff of my master plan of comedy.

13
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:34,080
Your what? Phase one, I ignored her.

14
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:37,600
Phase two, sat across from her in the lunchroom, never made eye contact.

15
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:41,860
Phase three, pulled some strings to get into her English class, sat behind her the

16
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,060
whole year, never talked to her once.

17
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:46,260
You've been doing this all semester.

18
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:47,780
Don't be silly.

19
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:48,920
It's in sixth grade.

20
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:56,000
It's definitely worth it, because now I have become that unattainable, desirable man

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,820
of mystery. Okay.

22
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,200
Oh, she wants me so bad.

23
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,860
What? What are you blind?

24
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,160
She practically undressed me with her eyes.

25
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,900
That little tease.

26
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,440
It's time to put that poor, love -starved girl out of her misery.

27
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,440
Hi, Ben. Hi, Cheryl.

28
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,800
Hey, what's going on?

29
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,100
What a coincidence running into you.

30
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,140
This is the 18th coincidence today.

31
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:28,280
Somehow I seem to have memorized your schedule.

32
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:32,600
You did? Look, Cheryl, can we talk later?

33
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,260
I'm kind of busy.

34
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:35,280
Too busy for our history presentation?

35
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,340
Our history presentation?

36
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:39,740
We signed up as partners in class last week.

37
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:40,880
I don't remember that.

38
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,220
You were sleeping.

39
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:43,440
I held up your hand.

40
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:47,300
So when do you want to get together to work on it?

41
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,220
After school? Not really.

42
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,300
Tonight? We'll discuss it.

43
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:55,740
Later tonight? Look, Cheryl, Luke and I have got some man things to talk about.

44
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,040
You know, spitting, scratching.

45
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:05,740
What? I also wanted to know, would you go to the Sadie Hawkins dance with me on

46
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:10,700
Saturday night? Uh, gee, I'd like to, but I think something might come up.

47
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:11,520
Is that a maybe?

48
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:13,220
No, I don't know.

49
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:16,100
I think that's the night my mom's having her surgery.

50
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:21,220
Really? What's wrong with her?

51
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:25,320
Nothing serious. She's donating the kidney.

52
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:27,240
Oh, my gosh, to who?

53
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,760
Oh, whoever pops up.

54
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:34,380
Wow, she's really generous.

55
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,620
Now I can see why you're so sweet.

56
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,000
Okay, then. I'll see.

57
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,680
Yeah, right. Bye.

58
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:47,740
Anyway, Sasha waits.

59
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,060
Won't kill her.

60
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,540
All right, I've let you dangle long enough.

61
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:59,220
Your hunk of hunk of burning love is here.

62
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:37,380
Oh But you and me, we gotta be the luckiest dreamers who never quit dreaming.

63
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:40,500
As long as we keep on giving,

64
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:44,980
we can take anything that comes our way.

65
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:54,120
Baby, rain or shine, all the time, we got each other sharing the laughter and love.

66
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,800
oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh This is big time.

67
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:28,340
I have to tell my class what your jobs are.

68
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:32,040
Well, honey, that sounds like fun, and we'll both help you.

69
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:33,840
So I'm stuck doing it.

70
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:40,100
Guess who got an A on her first lab assignment from Felix?

71
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,660
I flunked my mother, Fitzsimmons.

72
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,720
Chris, if you want help, there's the person to go to.

73
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,400
Help with what?

74
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:48,280
Chris, he just got her first homework assignment.

75
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:51,960
That's wonderful. I remember mine.

76
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:55,240
We had to describe our favorite time of year.

77
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:57,020
I chose winter.

78
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:01,460
All right. Then we had to have two parent -teacher conferences over that one.

79
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:06,760
I still can't believe that I was the only five -year -old to see Frosty the Snowman

80
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,820
as a metaphor for death.

81
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:12,700
I'll wait for Mike.

82
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:18,000
Dill chips, peanut butter, and mayonnaise.

83
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,500
Hey, guys. Hey, Mike, you want one of my miracle sandwiches?

84
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,520
What's the miracle?

85
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:25,480
You can swallow it without hurling.

86
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:30,900
Thanks anyway, but Kate's making a macrobiotic dinner for me tonight.

87
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,140
I gotta be totally starved to choke it down.

88
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:38,700
Hey, guys, there's a girl walking up the walk there.

89
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,040
She's kind of cute.

90
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:40,920
She's about your age.

91
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,400
She must be lost.

92
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,960
Oh, no, it's Cheryl Murray.

93
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,780
We're supposed to work on that stupid assignment.

94
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,600
What a pest.

95
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,100
Look, make an excuse for me.

96
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,760
Ben, there is no excuse for you.

97
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,080
What about your history project?

98
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:58,400
I'm not doing homework when I could be out living the wildlife.

99
00:05:58,580 --> 00:05:59,700
I'm going bowling with Stinky.

100
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:02,000
Does it get me better than that?

101
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:06,300
Hey, it must be Cheryl.

102
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:06,800
Come on in.

103
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,960
Uh, Ben had to run out.

104
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,800
Uh, he... he said that Luke would explain.

105
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,220
Uh, hi. Ben had to go to Stinky's.

106
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,020
It was an emergency.

107
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:19,340
Oh, gee. Anything serious?

108
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:22,040
Nah, emergencies happen a lot to guys named Stinky.

109
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,960
You don't have to cover for him.

110
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:27,960
It's me, isn't it?

111
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,320
He thinks I'm a dork.

112
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,820
Oh, no, he doesn't.

113
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,580
Really? He doesn't even think.

114
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,320
Well, I guess I'll work on my presentation along.

115
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,780
Well, what's it on?

116
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:43,400
The 500th anniversary of Columbus' voyage.

117
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,620
Thanks for reminding me, you know.

118
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:46,740
We still have to get him a gift.

119
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:51,820
Huh? Yeah, what does a 500 -year -old explorer need?

120
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:56,900
Mouth's mouth? Imagine how famous he'd be if he were alive today.

121
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,460
Cover of People magazine, doing lunch at the White House,

122
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,720
get shots on Hollywood squares.

123
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:04,860
I'll take Christopher Columbus to block.

124
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,300
He'd probably be selling his own line of perfume.

125
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:11,040
Chris Columbus's discovery.

126
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,640
A New World odor.

127
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:17,380
Today on Oprah, men who exploit the New World and the women who love them.

128
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:20,760
And of course he'd be in our sinew.

129
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,220
That's how you should do your project.

130
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,280
Yeah, like a talk show.

131
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:30,240
Ladies and gentlemen, he proved the world is bigger and rower than the Pillsbury

132
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:34,060
Doughboy's butt. Give it up for my man, Christopher Columbus.

133
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,980
Whoo -hoo -hoo -hoo -hoo -hoo.

134
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,680
Chris, two words.

135
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,140
New world, how did you do it?

136
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,620
Dedication, perseverance, and regular floggings.

137
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,160
I hear you.

138
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,740
Okay. You're an explorer.

139
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,560
Mm -hmm. You're a sailor.

140
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:56,720
You're a navigator.

141
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:00,180
What next? I want to direct.

142
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,640
We gotta take a break.

143
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,680
We'll be right back.

144
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,940
Whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo, whoo.

145
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,420
So Ben says people come into your office and they lay down on the couch.

146
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,720
Some people do, yes.

147
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,300
Do you make them take a nap?

148
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,560
No, no, no, they don't sleep.

149
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,540
The couch just helps them relax.

150
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:19,120
Is this before or after you shrunk their heads?

151
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:21,520
That's a figure of speech.

152
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,140
I just talk to them.

153
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,880
About what? Well, whatever they want to talk about.

154
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,360
Whatever they need to talk about.

155
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:32,880
A lady came in to see me yesterday because she was really upset with her husband.

156
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:36,280
Like Mommy? No, no.

157
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:38,260
This lady's upset all the time.

158
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,600
Oh, like Carol.

159
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,280
No. No, let's see.

160
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:47,180
Um, people think they know the reasons they do things, hmm?

161
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:51,900
But inside of every person, there's sort of a second person in there.

162
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,860
And that's the real reason we do things, see?

163
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:58,180
And these two people are always fighting with each other, trying to control the

164
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:05,260
third person. This would be easier if you understood the id, ego, and superego.

165
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,280
This would be easier if you were a fireman.

166
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:11,380
Oh man, I am starved.

167
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:14,400
I need something with meat or sugar or fat in it.

168
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:16,060
I thought you ate a Kate's.

169
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:20,220
Oh, well, we had, let's see, hay...

170
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:25,500
stucco patties... and for dessert, we split a chia pet.

171
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:32,340
Well, how about I make you a sandwich with no ingredients that occur in nature?

172
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:33,360
Oh, all right.

173
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,400
Now, that's food.

174
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:40,300
Mike, I need your advice about dating and Ben.

175
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:42,060
Oh, that's easy enough.

176
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:43,080
He's not your type.

177
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,680
I'm talking about Cheryl.

178
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,340
Oh, is that the girl that was here earlier?

179
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,820
Yeah. Anyway, she likes Ben.

180
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,640
Oh, so she's insane.

181
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:54,780
Maybe, but I like her.

182
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,400
And I think she likes me.

183
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:59,960
I mean, ever since she left, she's all I can think about.

184
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:04,480
And Ben, well, I get the impression he'd like her to disappear.

185
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:06,500
Yeah? What makes you think that?

186
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,300
Well, he said I wish he'd disappear.

187
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:11,460
Great. Then what's the problem?

188
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,020
I don't know the rules about dating.

189
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,480
Is it all right for me to see Cheryl again?

190
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:17,360
Yeah, that sounds great to me.

191
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:20,500
I mean, you get her, she gets you, and Ben gets Stinky.

192
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,660
Hey, nice sweater.

193
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:29,000
I got one just like it, only I never wear it.

194
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,200
Makes me look like a dork.

195
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:32,040
Actually, this is your sweater.

196
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:33,800
I mean, I didn't think you'd mind.

197
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,480
Everybody says it makes you look like a dork.

198
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,720
Hey, there she is.

199
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:41,860
So, how's this sound?

200
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:46,520
So, Sasha, do you want anything special Saturday night between eight and midnight?

201
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:47,540
What do you think?

202
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,180
Nice balance between subtlety and begging.

203
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:54,120
Oh, no, not now.

204
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,300
It's Cheryl. At least I think it's Cheryl.

205
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,360
She looks so girl -like.

206
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,640
Look, do me a favor.

207
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,920
Keep her busy so she doesn't blow my chances with Sasha.

208
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,020
Gotta go to class.

209
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,120
Hi, Ben. Hi, Luke.

210
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,860
Uh, Cheryl, um, I gotta run.

211
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,540
Luke was just asking me about my schedule.

212
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:11,880
Maybe you could fill him in?

213
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:17,360
Hi, Sasha. And speaking of the Sadie Hawkins dance...

214
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,180
Me and you?

215
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,340
What are you, joking?

216
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,840
Not in a million years.

217
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,460
Don't ever speak to me again.

218
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,440
Hey, I already have a date for the dance.

219
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,160
Just quit throwing yourself at me.

220
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,460
It's over, baby.

221
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:38,720
So, Cheryl, I've got some good news.

222
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,620
They found some of your mom's kidney?

223
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:44,780
No, uh, actually, nobody needed it, so they put it back.

224
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:48,320
Uh -huh. So, uh, now I can go to the dance with you.

225
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:52,360
Gee, Ben, I'm sorry, but since you didn't give me an answer, I'm going with Luke.

226
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:01,960
Okay, come on, Chrissy.

227
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:04,280
The best way to learn about my job is to help me do it.

228
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,660
Now, I'm writing an article for the newspaper.

229
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,300
About murders and stuff?

230
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:10,980
No, but it's very important.

231
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:14,380
About what? Boxer shorts.

232
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:23,900
Oh, really? Honey, a consumer reporter tests different products to tell people which

233
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:24,720
ones they should buy.

234
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,380
Today, it's men's boxer shorts.

235
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,820
Happy man boxer shorts.

236
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:32,620
If what's inside your shorts really matters,

237
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,680
only happy man shorts will do.

238
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:39,180
Uh, uh, okay, let's test the waistband.

239
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:43,580
Ouch. The elastic has to be strong.

240
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,160
Who wants their shorts around their ankles?

241
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:50,060
Not me. They also claim to be specially treated to resist stains.

242
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,640
Well, we shall see.

243
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:58,060
This is a lot more from a daddy's job.

244
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:02,680
Okay, we'll finish up later.

245
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:03,680
Let's get dinner out of the oven.

246
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,980
Where's Luke? Oh, I think he's...

247
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:11,920
Luke!...upstairs. Luke!

248
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:17,800
Good pipes. Every Luke with little five miles is on his way over.

249
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:22,400
I can't believe you humiliated me in front of the entire school.

250
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:25,820
What? You know Cheryl Murray was my territory.

251
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:28,500
Your territory, you treat her like dog dirt.

252
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:30,640
We've got a special relationship.

253
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,180
It's none of your business.

254
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:35,880
Oh, yeah? Well, I'm making it my business.

255
00:13:36,060 --> 00:13:38,720
I'm the guy who's taking her to the Sadie Hawkins dance.

256
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,240
Yeah, over my dead body.

257
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,280
